<title>USA: FoxMeyer to auction off assets before Nov 8.</title>
<headline>FoxMeyer to auction off assets before Nov 8.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>FoxMeyer Drug Co is getting ready to conduct an auction of its assets under the U.S. Bankruptcy Code prior to a hearing to consider the sale, the company said.</p>
<p>A U.S. Bankruptcy Court in Delaware issued an order approving the auction, setting a November 8 hearing on the approval of the sale of the FoxMeyer's assets and its affiliated companies, it said in a statement sent to Reuters.</p>
<p>The hearing will consider the sale of the assets to McKesson Corp or to a higher bidder, it added.</p>
<p>McKesson had earlier agreed to buy the assets for about $80 million in cash.</p>
<p>FoxMeyer is the fourth largest pharmaceutical and health- care products distributor in North America.</p>
</text>
